# Segment words, `notrack` and lone prefix words in 16-bit code (.code16): the
# statements of segment-words.casefile where real-mode code has them, each
# held to GNU as 2.47.
#
# Not here: a segment word on a direct `call` (see segment-words.casefile),
# and `cs jecxz`, where GNU as writes the address-size prefix in front of the
# segment (67 2e e3) and lccc the segment first, as everywhere else.
;;; cs_nop
.text
.code16
cs nop
;;; ds_nop
.text
.code16
ds nop
